  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal Express obligated $75.3M in FY2027 to date across 50 awards, with an average award size of $1.5M. Obligations fell 80.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows peaks and troughs: FY24 obligations were $677M, FY25 obligations were $582M, FY26 obligations were $383M, FY23 obligations were $275M, and FY22 obligations were $309M. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the vast majority of FY2027 to date obligations with $75.2M. Other agencies recorded much smaller FY2027 to date buys, including the Department of the Treasury at $80.6K, the Department of Justice at $8.9K, the Railroad Retirement Board at $2.8K, and the Court Services and Offender Supervision Agency at $2.5K. The Department of Commerce and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration show $0 in FY2027 to date obligations. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity rather than a full fiscal year.",
